@facebook @Meta @GoI_MeitY — First demonetisation, now restricted access in India. Why must a journalist repeatedly fight to keep his platform functioning?

Just days ago, Facebook demonetised my “Ambuj Kumar – Lokhit India” Page. Monetisation was restored after I complained and raised questions. Now, on 9 November 2026, Facebook has notified me of a 7-day restriction on my account in India, alongside separate notices restricting access to my Page, a video and a photograph.

Facebook attributes these actions to local legal requirements and a notice from the “Government of India / Law Enforcement.” Its messages cite Section 79(3)(b) of the IT Act and Rule 4(4) of the IT Rules, 2021.

Yet I have not been given the underlying government notice or complaint. Which agency sought this action? Which specific content is objectionable, and on what precise legal grounds? These details have not been disclosed to me. Merely naming a legal provision is not accountability.

The affected material includes a news video posted on 26 September and a photograph identifying my news platform, posted on 16 June. What justifies restricting that photograph?

I seek clear answers:

Who issued the notice? Provide the agency’s name, the date, the reference number and a copy.
Which specific statement or part of each post allegedly violates which law?
Facebook claims earlier warnings were issued. When and where were they sent? Provide the records.
What justifies restricting an entire account/Page over objections to individual posts?
Was the material and its journalistic context reviewed by a human?
Will there be a transparent review of these separate actions—demonetisation, restoration following my complaint, and now restricted access?
What exactly will be restored after 7 days, and what effective appeal process is available?

I am not claiming that the two actions share a common cause. But repeated disruptions directly affect my journalism, livelihood and ability to reach my audience.

Independent journalism cannot be left at the mercy of vague notifications and opaque decisions. I demand disclosure of the underlying notice and specific reasons, an urgent human review, and restoration of access to my account/Page.

My Page: https://t.co/ERBRibgfO6

